<section class="legal-shell"><p class="landing-kicker">Privacy</p><h1>Your repository remains your repository.</h1><p>WTFCode stores your account, repository URL, project metadata, derived dependency information, detected symbol names and signatures, bounded relationship evidence excerpts, exploration progress, and scan findings. Complete source files are not retained in the application database. Derived evidence can still be sensitive.</p><p>In production, each scan uses a temporary checkout, removed after the worker finishes. A source or Git view may create a temporary checkout removed after the request. Local development retains checkouts for debugging. Questions use the local deterministic engine; customer questions do not invoke external AI providers. Private repository access is disabled by default pending verification.</p><h2>Your account controls</h2><p>Signed-in users can <a href="<?= e(url('account.php')) ?>">export account and project metadata or delete their account</a>. Deletion removes active records and queues temporary storage cleanup. Encrypted backups may retain deleted records until their retention period ends; restored backups require deletion reconciliation before service resumes.</p><h2>Verification, recovery and optional feedback</h2><p>Account links expire and work once. Only token digests are stored in the database. Delivery requests retain the recipient address while the worker retries and are scheduled for deletion after 24 hours. Optional feedback stores a category, product area and usefulness rating with your account for 30 days, then worker maintenance removes it. Retention cleanup requires a running worker. It is included in your export and deleted with your account. The feedback form accepts no source code or credentials. No third-party analytics are added.</p><h2>Before external pilot access</h2><p>The founder must supply and approve the operator identity, support/privacy contact, backup retention and legal notices. The proposed backup retention is seven days; no hosted backup schedule or live email delivery is asserted by this preview. Do not import confidential source. Private imports remain disabled.</p></section>
